# Environment variables
#
# `.env*.local` was too narrow, and that is not a style opinion — it is the exact reason a real
# credentials file reached git history on 2026-09-03/04: the backup was named
# `.env.local.before-icloud-username-fix`, and the old pattern requires the name to END in `.local`,
# so the file was never ignored (found by gitleaks 2026-09-18, 90 findings across 9 commits).
# Every spelling of an environment file is ignored now; the committed example is the one exception.
.env*
!.env.example

# Local pnpm store (workspace-local store used by the sandboxed toolchain)
.pnpm-store/

# Agent worker scheduler local overrides (optional, machine-specific)
.env.scheduler

