.serena/

# Forge generated lane state: rtk command shims (git/ls/tree/gh) and the workspace
# skill dir. These are written INTO the worktree by writeRtkShims on every lane start,
# so leaving them untracked-but-unignored put `.forge/rtk-bin/*` into a candidate
# commit (seen live 2026-09-13 on ENG-FORGE-SMOKE-01) — generated files in every
# story's diff, and a scope check asked to explain files the role never wrote.
/.forge/

# Agent-tool config directories. Measured 2026-09-15: 50+ of these existed as untracked
# directories at the repo root (`git status` printed 58 untracked entries, and the noise
# is where a real stray file hides), each written by a different CLI's bootstrap. They are
# per-machine tool state, not this project's source: no rule, packet or gate reads them, and
# `docs/agent/VENDOR-ADAPTERS.md` already says the handbook lives in AGENTS.md. The one that
# matters — CLAUDE.md — stays tracked on purpose, because its generated block is gated.
# Force-add a specific path (git add -f) if a tool's config ever becomes project history.
