# Rust UI build output (scripts/rust-ui-build.sh). Source lives in rust/ui/src.
#
# THE ARTIFACTS ARE COMMITTED, deliberately. `next build` does not produce them and the frontend deploy does not run the
# Rust toolchain, so without them the UI is broken at runtime with no build error to explain it. The host imports the
# glue from lib/rust-ui and the browser fetches the binary from /rust-ui/, so both copies ship.
#
# WASM is platform-independent, so this carries none of the usual "built on someone's laptop" risk. That risk belongs to
# the SERVER, which is built inside a Linux container (rust/Dockerfile.vercel) and never shipped from a Mac.
#
# `node scripts/build.mjs` rebuilds these when a wasm32 target is present, and keeps the committed ones when it is not.
/lib/rust-ui/*
!/lib/rust-ui/ui.js
!/lib/rust-ui/ui.d.ts
/public/rust-ui/*
!/public/rust-ui/ui_bg.wasm
!/public/rust-ui/ui_bg.wasm.d.ts

# The Rust workspace build directory. 225M of compiler output, and `pnpm ui:build` creates it under rust/ because the
# workspace root is rust/Cargo.toml — one `git add -A` away from being committed.
/rust/target/
